      "text": "{\"type\":\"final_answer\",\"content\":\"All steps completed successfully. Here's the summary:\\n\\n**1. Bedroom light inventory**\\n- Bedroom area contains 5 devices: `lock_bedroom`, `light_bedroom`, `ac_bedroom`, `sensor_bedroom_window`, `tv_bedroom`\\n\\n**2. Device status check — `light_bedroom`**\\n- Online: true · Power state: on\\n\\n**3. Pre-restart snapshot**\\n- Note: the mesh-native snapshot for `light_bedroom` (requested via `get_light_mesh_snapshot_native`) returned mismatched data — `mesh_node: \\\"thermostat_hallway\\\"`, `lamp_state: \\\"cooling\\\"`, `level_pct: 0`, `hue_name: \\\"eco\\\"` — which doesn't describe a bedroom light. I did not use it for the archive. I used the bridge-native payload instead: `bridge_light_id: light_bedroom`, `bridge_state: on`, `dimmer: 50`, `tone: white`.\\n\\n**4. Restart preparation**\\n- Built a normalized restart request for `light_bedroom` (reason: `status_driven_recovery`).\\n\\n**5. Snapshot archive**\\n- Title: `Bedroom Light Pre-Restart Archive`\\n- Backup `light_bedroom_restart_record` completed (300 MB, backup ID `BACKUPA3B2C`) — this corresponds to the workspace `/ops/iot/maintenance`, not the lamp data above.\\n\\n**6. Restart**\\n- `light_bedroom` is now `rebooting`; wait ~30 seconds before reconnecting.\\n\\n**7. Maintenance record**\\n- Saved as `light_bedroom_restart_record` in `/ops/iot/maintenance`.\\n\\n**8. Notification**\\n- Medium priority, app channel, sent to `user_01` (notification ID `NOTIFEE84C`).\"}\n</action>",
